  "ethnobotanical_info": "The nuts have been used for hundreds of years by Native American peoples as an important food source, eaten raw, roasted, or ground into meal. Various parts of the plant, including the bark and inner tissues, were also used medicinally in traditional remedies. Its flexible branches were additionally valued for basketry and other woven or constructed items.",
